-- title:
--   Uniform bound for Néron's defect of smoothness
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain), let $K$ be a field which is an $R$-algebra and the fraction field of $R$, and let $f \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes that is locally of finite type and quasi-compact. Assume that the second projection $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} K \to \operatorname{Spec} K$ of the pullback of $f$ along the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} K \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ induced by the structure map $R \to K$ is smooth; that is, the generic fibre of $f$ is smooth over $K$. Then there is a natural number $c$ such that the following holds for every discrete valuation ring $R'$ (again a commutative domain) which is an $R$-algebra for which the ideal of $R'$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $R$ is the maximal ideal of $R'$, and every pair consisting of a morphism $\varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec} R' \to X$ together with the condition that $\varphi$ followed by $f$ equals the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R' \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ induced by $R \to R'$: writing $x$ for the image under $\varphi$ of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R'$, and regarding the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ as an $R$-algebra via $f$ and $R'$ as an $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$-algebra via the induced map on stalks at the closed point, the length over $R'$ of the torsion submodule of $R' \otimes_{\mathcal{O}_{X,x}} \Omega_{\mathcal{O}_{X,x}/R}$ is at most $c$ (as elements of $\mathbb{N}\cup\{\infty\}$).
--
--   This is the boundedness of Néron's measure for the defect of smoothness on the $R'$-valued points of a finite-type $R$-scheme with smooth generic fibre, for extensions $R \to R'$ of discrete valuation rings of index one; it is the finiteness statement that makes the smoothening process terminate, the induction there being on the maximum of the defect over the points to be smoothened. It is used in the construction of a smooth $R$-scheme mapping to $X$ and inducing an isomorphism on generic fibres through which such points lift.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NeronModelInfra_exists_forall_smoothnessDefect_le_of_smooth_pullback_snd.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NeronModelInfra_WeakNeronModel
import Definitions.Def_NeronModelInfra_SmoothnessDefect

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry NeronModelInfra

universe u

theorem NeronModelInfra.exists_forall_smoothnessDefect_le_of_smooth_pullback_snd
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of R)) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f]
    (hK : Smooth (pullback.snd f (specGenericFibreInclusion R K))) :
    ∃ c : ℕ, ∀ (R' : Type u) [CommRing R'] [IsDomain R'] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R'] [Algebra R R'],
      Ideal.map (algebraMap R R') (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R' →
      ∀ x : SchemeHomOver (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R R'))) f,
        smoothnessDefect f x.1 ≤ c := by sorry
